From 400928c4dde4e0fba9606179c0332e938b4396a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonas=20=C3=85dahl?= <jadahl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:54:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] daemon/system: Gracefully handling the session going
 away

If the session outlives the remote client, we'd have a weak ref for a
session that is associated with an already-freed remote client,
when the session is later disposed, this would cause a use-after-free.

Fix this by removing the weak ref when freeing the remote client.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-remote-desktop/-/merge_requests/411>
---
