Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:57:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Support Kerberos based remote login

This fully performs the Kerberos authentication, mapping a resolved
Kerberos principal with a local user account. A remote display manager
display is created with this user set as 'preauthenticated', allowing
GDM to bypass any additional authentication.

This does not yet make use of any TGT (ticket granting ticket)
mechanisms, but makes GDM fully trust gnome-remote-desktop's system
daemon to have performed the user authentication.

Configuration is done the same way as when configuring Kerberos
authentication for the single user headless session.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-remote-desktop/-/merge_requests/411>
